WEBVTT

00:00.460 --> 00:03.250
Slay the dragon and keep your promise,

00:03.250 --> 00:04.800
my knight.

00:05.990 --> 00:09.160
On my sword, on the light,

00:09.160 --> 00:12.560
on the souls of the warriors 
that dwell within my chest...

00:12.980 --> 00:16.020
I will slay the evil dragon!

00:24.290 --> 00:29.840
The Faraway Paladin

00:26.130 --> 00:29.840
<b><u>The Lord of the Rust Mountains</u></b>

01:47.160 --> 01:52.000
Calldawn

01:52.010 --> 01:54.510
Burn, flames of courage!

01:54.510 --> 01:56.260
The time for retribution has come!

01:56.260 --> 01:58.000
Evil ends now!

01:58.130 --> 02:00.510
<b>Warrior! Warrior!</b>

01:58.130 --> 02:00.510
Bellator! Bellator!

02:00.510 --> 02:03.510
<b>Fortis fortuna adiuvat!</b>

02:00.510 --> 02:03.510
Fortune favors the bold!

02:22.100 --> 02:23.450
Divine protection of light!

02:41.160 --> 02:43.090
I will crush you!

02:45.380 --> 02:46.010
Will!

02:46.010 --> 02:46.840
Sir Will!

02:55.760 --> 02:57.110
I swear, Will...

02:58.360 --> 03:00.310
He's grown accustomed to his movements.

03:06.110 --> 03:08.620
That comes with a bonus gift of hydra venom!

03:14.770 --> 03:16.010
Fire!

03:21.500 --> 03:23.180
Charge!

03:29.990 --> 03:31.270
Defend!

03:31.930 --> 03:35.620
Burn, flames of courage!

03:44.430 --> 03:48.590
We will take back our homeland!

03:58.250 --> 04:02.380
I didn't want to do this, as it 
would also harm my treasure...

04:02.670 --> 04:04.680
If he breathes that stuff at us, it's over!

04:04.910 --> 04:06.380
Brave warriors,

04:06.380 --> 04:09.150
this shall bring your demise!

04:07.930 --> 04:09.680
<b>Maximum Accelerate!</b>

04:07.930 --> 04:09.840
Maxima Acceleratio!

04:16.190 --> 04:18.290
Solis Ortus!

04:16.440 --> 04:17.690
<b>Rise, Sun!</b>

04:47.820 --> 04:50.360
<i>If I go down with the dragon, 
that's just fine.</i>

04:50.360 --> 04:51.990
<i>You must not give up.</i>

05:09.730 --> 05:11.980
<i>I swore to the goddess...</i>

05:12.540 --> 05:18.250
<i>that I would not give up on 
life until the very end!</i>

05:25.760 --> 05:28.320
Will! Hey, Will!

05:28.320 --> 05:29.420
Sir Will!

05:33.020 --> 05:34.030
Huh?

05:34.420 --> 05:35.470
I...

05:35.470 --> 05:37.430
Hey, can you talk?

05:37.430 --> 05:39.360
Will, do you know what's going on?

05:40.260 --> 05:43.420
I'm fine, Menel.

05:47.210 --> 05:48.740
Don't get up yet.

05:49.460 --> 05:53.100
No. I feel really good, for some reason.

06:16.480 --> 06:17.840
You saved us.

06:17.840 --> 06:19.720
Thank you.

06:19.720 --> 06:21.420
I appreciate your aid.

06:22.430 --> 06:26.660
Farewell, my friends, my precursors.

06:26.660 --> 06:30.500
The young master and I 
will take over from here.

06:30.780 --> 06:34.870
I will restore the Iron Country 
to its former glory.

06:49.270 --> 06:50.250
What's wrong?

06:50.250 --> 06:53.400
My body... seems weird.

06:53.400 --> 06:57.640
No kidding. Do you know how many 
times you were turned to charcoal?

06:57.640 --> 06:58.770
Just rest.

06:58.770 --> 07:01.140
No, I don't mean like that.

07:05.320 --> 07:06.430
Hey...

07:07.510 --> 07:08.140
Huh?!

07:10.840 --> 07:12.340
What is this?

07:12.340 --> 07:15.620
You sucked up the dragon's life 
force through your demonblade.

07:15.620 --> 07:17.120
It should be no surprise.

07:17.120 --> 07:22.250
Your body and soul were burned 
red-hot by the dragon's breath,

07:22.250 --> 07:25.620
tempering you, 
and his blood then hardened you.

07:25.620 --> 07:26.710
Uh, what?

07:26.710 --> 07:28.100
To put it plainly,

07:28.100 --> 07:32.880
Valacirca's dragon factor has interwoven 
itself deeply into your body and soul.

07:33.230 --> 07:36.310
Ordinary blades can no longer cut you,

07:36.310 --> 07:40.640
and weak Words will feel like 
no more than a light breeze.

07:40.640 --> 07:41.960
Um...

07:41.960 --> 07:45.800
However, this state does bring about 
an increase in one's animal nature.

07:46.640 --> 07:48.510
Do not let this power make you arrogant,

07:48.510 --> 07:51.710
but make every effort to keep 
the dragon factor quiet.

07:51.710 --> 07:55.180
If you do not, it will bring you to ruin.

07:55.180 --> 07:59.170
And I do not wish to see you 
die such a pitiful death.

07:59.170 --> 08:00.660
Stagnate...

08:04.980 --> 08:07.920
I carelessly used my power.

08:08.150 --> 08:12.820
But then, as I helped you slay 
the dragon, you now owe me.

08:12.820 --> 08:14.960
It was not a bad trade-off.

08:14.960 --> 08:17.520
You do feel indebted to me, do you not?

08:17.520 --> 08:18.540
Yes.

08:18.540 --> 08:19.990
Good.

08:19.990 --> 08:22.730
When dealing with a hero such as yourself,

08:22.730 --> 08:25.110
pinning you down and forcing you to yield

08:25.110 --> 08:29.430
is less effective than making you 
feel grateful and indebted to me.

08:29.690 --> 08:34.200
It is a shame that Gracefeel guided 
those dwarf warriors away,

08:34.200 --> 08:37.180
but why seek them out simply 
to make trouble for you

08:37.180 --> 08:40.520
when asking for nothing and making 
you more and more indebted to me

08:40.520 --> 08:42.590
will prove more profitable later?

08:42.970 --> 08:45.940
That's exactly what scares me about you.

08:47.190 --> 08:49.420
Then I shall go now.

08:49.420 --> 08:52.970
And farewell to you, Gracefeel. 
I have troubled you on this occasion.

08:53.410 --> 08:55.470
Stagnate, goddess of the undead...

08:55.670 --> 09:00.180
Will you not consider giving up on 
your ideal? It is not too late.

09:00.180 --> 09:02.100
Would you discard your undead powers

09:02.100 --> 09:05.470
and work with me to guide souls once more?

09:05.470 --> 09:07.140
If you would—

09:07.140 --> 09:10.460
Don't finish that thought. 
And no, I will not.

09:10.460 --> 09:13.230
I will follow my own ideals.

09:14.550 --> 09:15.990
I see.

09:15.990 --> 09:18.250
Farewell, my elder sister.

09:18.250 --> 09:21.830
Yes. Farewell, my little sister.

09:23.530 --> 09:26.840
Well, then, William G. Maryblood...

09:27.250 --> 09:30.550
You now shine even more brightly as a hero,

09:30.550 --> 09:33.030
and you have acquired great power.

09:33.030 --> 09:36.300
But as light grows, 
so too does the darkness.

09:36.300 --> 09:39.510
Do try to avoid becoming war-crazed 
and detesting people,

09:39.510 --> 09:41.760
and keep your womanizing in check...

09:41.760 --> 09:45.230
Oh, dear, that's right. 
You don't have a woman, do you?

09:45.230 --> 09:47.010
Mind your own business!

09:47.800 --> 09:51.450
I understand that you have 
devoted yourself to my sister,

09:51.450 --> 09:54.290
but you should have at least one mate.

09:54.290 --> 09:58.180
How else will I have the pleasure 
of seducing your offspring?

09:58.180 --> 10:00.280
That's the worst reason you 
could give for saying that.

10:00.280 --> 10:01.520
In fact...

10:01.520 --> 10:04.670
If I create a female Echo one day,

10:04.670 --> 10:07.040
would you care to produce offspring with me?

10:08.810 --> 10:12.080
I am not requesting that you do so for me,

10:12.080 --> 10:14.150
but what harm could one child do?

10:14.150 --> 10:18.190
Rhea Silvia creates demigod children 
with heroes all the time.

10:21.810 --> 10:24.560
Very well. I will give up for now.

10:24.990 --> 10:26.050
Also...

10:26.050 --> 10:30.970
I once asked if you would like 
me to love you, did I not?

10:31.460 --> 10:33.200
That was a lie.

10:53.470 --> 10:58.510
I do love you, William G. Maryblood.

11:05.590 --> 11:07.030
Um...

11:07.620 --> 11:10.300
Man, goddesses sure are impetuous.

11:10.300 --> 11:12.610
Be happy, Will.

11:14.330 --> 11:17.700
My knight, and you heroes,

11:17.700 --> 11:20.070
you have done well to slay the evil dragon.

11:20.700 --> 11:22.350
Splendid work.

11:23.760 --> 11:25.800
<i>I really can't believe we won.</i>

11:26.460 --> 11:29.250
I shall reward your efforts.

11:29.250 --> 11:31.760
If there is anything you desire, speak.

11:32.540 --> 11:34.020
A wish...

11:34.020 --> 11:35.510
If I may...

11:35.770 --> 11:37.450
Goddess of light,

11:37.450 --> 11:40.030
would it be possible to expel 
the evil dragon's miasma

11:40.030 --> 11:43.020
from the area around these 
mountains, including Lothdor?

11:43.020 --> 11:45.250
Now that the evil dragon is gone,

11:45.250 --> 11:48.770
this request can be granted, to an extent.

11:52.120 --> 11:53.990
Then I ask you:

11:53.990 --> 11:56.770
please purify our homeland!

11:56.770 --> 11:59.350
I'll ask that as my request, too.

11:59.350 --> 12:01.400
Gotta think about Dine and her people.

12:02.050 --> 12:07.030
I make the same request, for the 
sake of my fallen compatriots.

12:07.030 --> 12:09.290
I'm fine with that, too.

12:09.290 --> 12:12.280
Just being able to fight the 
dragon was enough for me.

12:14.310 --> 12:15.530
Then I also....

12:15.870 --> 12:18.550
request your purification and blessing.

12:18.550 --> 12:22.220
I have heard your wishes.

12:29.170 --> 12:32.030
Sorrow for those who have been lost...

12:32.700 --> 12:35.100
Blessings upon those who are born...

12:35.550 --> 12:40.960
Peace, prosperity, and joy upon the land.

12:48.550 --> 12:50.890
Heroes who have slain the dragon,

12:51.380 --> 12:54.940
you who have reclaimed and 
restored this land...

12:54.940 --> 12:58.210
May the blessing of the 
light be with you always.

13:09.460 --> 13:11.740
Let's clean up here and head home.

13:11.740 --> 13:14.970
Of course. You should get 
some rest, Sir Will.

13:14.970 --> 13:16.640
We'll handle the rest.

13:16.640 --> 13:18.190
No, I can't—

13:17.530 --> 13:19.370
Just rest, damn it.

13:19.370 --> 13:22.120
You're way too reckless, you know.

13:22.120 --> 13:26.320
For real. I wasn't expecting you to 
take a swing at a time like that.

13:27.280 --> 13:29.710
It was a brilliant slash, though.

13:29.950 --> 13:35.700
Indeed. I don't think I'll ever forget 
that flash, bright as sunlight.

13:36.530 --> 13:38.820
We must celebrate our victory 
when we return home.

13:38.820 --> 13:39.810
Sounds good.

13:39.810 --> 13:43.440
We can invite the people of Lothdor 
and have them play music for us.

13:43.440 --> 13:47.270
That sounds wonderful! 
And we'll have food and drink, too!

13:47.270 --> 13:50.840
Tonio and Bee probably have 
it all prepared already.

13:50.840 --> 13:52.530
We can celebrate to our hearts' content.

13:53.310 --> 13:55.490
I'm starting to look forward to it!

14:07.600 --> 14:13.790
We took a few of the dragon's scales and 
his treasure as proof of our conquest

14:14.250 --> 14:16.290
and returned to town for a time.

14:31.080 --> 14:32.530
Hey!

14:35.600 --> 14:37.190
You're safe?!

14:37.190 --> 14:39.820
Well, yeah. Can't you tell?

14:39.820 --> 14:43.830
I heard the dragon's roar, 
and then suddenly, all was silent.

14:43.830 --> 14:47.170
Then a strange fire spread, 
and the entire area was cleansed...

14:49.070 --> 14:52.320
Truly... I am so glad!

15:06.910 --> 15:09.950
I thought perhaps you wouldn't return.

15:09.950 --> 15:13.270
I'm not gonna die. I still have stuff to do.

15:13.270 --> 15:14.420
Like what?

15:14.420 --> 15:17.700
Well, rebuilding this place, for starters.

15:17.700 --> 15:20.940
The after-effects of the dragon's 
miasma are still hanging on, right?

15:20.940 --> 15:25.560
True. The miasma isn't completely gone.

15:25.560 --> 15:27.450
There are still surviving demons, too.

15:27.820 --> 15:30.720
You'll give some of the 
dragon's treasure to us?

15:30.720 --> 15:34.080
Yes. There's more than enough of it.

15:34.080 --> 15:36.140
Use it to rebuild for the time being.

15:36.610 --> 15:39.570
But I fear that would be...

15:39.570 --> 15:42.320
I think we should take him up on his offer.

15:42.320 --> 15:44.350
Now that we've taken back the mountains,

15:44.350 --> 15:47.810
the former residents of the Iron 
Country will surely return, as well.

15:48.340 --> 15:52.600
We should work together to restore 
our land to its former prosperity.

15:55.470 --> 15:57.670
But we don't want an influx of wealth

15:57.670 --> 16:00.530
throwing off the balance of money and goods.

16:00.530 --> 16:02.600
Consult with Tonio first.

16:02.600 --> 16:03.550
Sure.

16:03.550 --> 16:07.020
We'll need to be ready to 
take in new residents, too.

16:07.020 --> 16:09.740
We won't run out of things 
to do anytime soon.

16:09.740 --> 16:12.080
I don't really want to,

16:12.080 --> 16:14.500
but I guess I'll drop by the 
forest where I was born

16:14.500 --> 16:18.320
and ask if they'll send some 
skilled folks to help.

16:18.320 --> 16:20.370
Then, I'll go with you.

16:20.370 --> 16:21.560
You will?

16:21.560 --> 16:25.100
The one making the request should 
be there to plead in person.

16:25.100 --> 16:27.180
Yeah, I guess so.

16:27.830 --> 16:30.260
Guess we'll cross the ocean 
once spring comes, then.

16:30.630 --> 16:32.350
I gotta go with you, huh?

16:31.750 --> 16:33.450
Just admit you're happy!

16:53.650 --> 16:54.720
Gus!

16:54.720 --> 16:56.400
Wandering Sage!

16:58.160 --> 17:01.160
You're all here! You didn't die?!

17:02.640 --> 17:05.380
The flow of your mana seems odd.

17:05.380 --> 17:06.890
A dragon factor?

17:08.130 --> 17:09.790
Nailed it, as always.

17:18.800 --> 17:21.220
That is a curse, you know.

17:21.220 --> 17:23.990
I know. And I accept it.

17:23.990 --> 17:27.250
Well, as long as you understand.

17:27.250 --> 17:30.310
More importantly, go on and let them know.

17:30.310 --> 17:31.130
Yeah.

17:33.810 --> 17:35.330
<i>I'm home.</i>

17:35.330 --> 17:38.040
<i>I made it back from defeating the dragon.</i>

17:38.620 --> 17:40.830
<i>You two saved me again.</i>

17:41.400 --> 17:42.500
<i>Thank you.</i>

17:47.580 --> 17:50.210
Allow me to return the weapon you lent me.

17:50.210 --> 17:54.710
No need for that. Keep it. 
I have no use for it.

17:54.710 --> 17:58.470
But isn't it a memento 
of your beloved comrade?

18:00.050 --> 18:02.970
How very sincere you are.

18:03.360 --> 18:05.880
It is because it belonged to my comrade

18:05.880 --> 18:09.490
that I cannot bring myself to 
let it rot away in storage.

18:09.490 --> 18:12.240
In that case, I accept 
this gift with gratitude.

18:12.500 --> 18:16.770
Indeed. I'm sure there could be 
no greater honor for that weapon

18:16.770 --> 18:19.480
than to serve the new king of the dwarfs.

18:19.480 --> 18:20.480
Oh...

18:21.840 --> 18:23.170
I'll return Calldawn.

18:23.500 --> 18:26.230
That sword belongs to you, Sir Will.

18:26.230 --> 18:30.360
No, I couldn't. It's been treasured 
by the dwarfs for generations.

18:30.360 --> 18:32.250
And they entrusted it to you.

18:32.510 --> 18:35.260
Fierce battles are a hero's destiny.

18:35.260 --> 18:38.240
Please make good use of that sword.

18:42.110 --> 18:44.140
I'll take good care of it on loan

18:44.140 --> 18:47.180
and return it to the Iron Country one day.

18:47.180 --> 18:47.920
Right!

18:47.920 --> 18:53.390
That makes it sound like even more 
tough enemies will be coming my way...

18:55.740 --> 18:56.890
Hello?!

18:56.890 --> 19:00.100
Well, you know... Live strong.

19:00.100 --> 19:01.920
I'll help you out a bit.

19:01.920 --> 19:04.530
That doesn't make me feel much better...

19:08.850 --> 19:10.320
Jeez!

19:21.720 --> 19:24.670
Welcome back! How did it go?

19:32.860 --> 19:35.010
We have slain the demons in the mountains,

19:35.010 --> 19:38.440
as well as the evil dragon, Valacirca!

19:45.150 --> 19:47.020
Congratulations!

19:46.050 --> 19:47.020
Bee!

19:48.180 --> 19:51.100
And everyone's okay? That's great!

19:51.100 --> 19:53.160
Wait, that's a dragon horn, isn't it?

19:53.490 --> 19:56.260
Let me see! I'm gonna write a song about it!

19:56.620 --> 19:58.430
Whoa, what's that? New equipment?

19:58.430 --> 20:01.100
It's awesome! Where did you get it?!

20:02.760 --> 20:04.040
Young master...

20:04.040 --> 20:06.510
You have grown into a fine man.

20:06.510 --> 20:09.180
There are so many things I 
want to tell all of you.

20:09.450 --> 20:11.440
About the Iron Country,

20:11.440 --> 20:13.460
about its brave warriors,

20:13.970 --> 20:16.020
and about our great king.

20:28.900 --> 20:30.700
It's good to see you back.

20:31.840 --> 20:32.620
Yeah.

20:33.210 --> 20:37.160
All right, now. Our lord and 
his companions must be tired.

20:37.160 --> 20:40.650
They've just returned from 
defeating a dragon, after all.

20:40.650 --> 20:43.220
We must give them some time to rest...

20:43.220 --> 20:45.790
and then kick off the party tomorrow!

20:46.040 --> 20:47.670
We're celebrating the dragon's defeat.

20:47.670 --> 20:51.320
Tomorrow, you can all eat, drink, 
and sing to your hearts' content,

20:51.320 --> 20:53.290
and help us celebrate!

22:31.840 --> 22:34.050
I'll give you a demon beast's head!

22:34.050 --> 22:36.090
D-Don't do it, Glen.

22:36.090 --> 22:37.380
It's dangerous.

22:37.380 --> 22:39.510
Shut up, Alex! Don't stop me!

22:39.510 --> 22:41.330
Are you adventurers?

22:42.140 --> 22:43.820
So what if we are?

22:44.080 --> 22:46.190
You can't handle the quests offered here.

22:46.710 --> 22:49.010
You should try that shop over there.

22:49.010 --> 22:50.190
What?!

22:50.190 --> 22:51.430
Who are you?

22:51.430 --> 22:55.280
And don't hold back on spending 
money on good equipment.

22:55.280 --> 22:56.380
Something like...

23:02.880 --> 23:05.640
Oh, wow! It has Signs!

23:05.640 --> 23:07.080
A magic dagger?!

23:07.080 --> 23:08.220
It's yours.

23:08.220 --> 23:10.340
It has Words of Light engraved in it,

23:10.340 --> 23:12.290
so it'll work in place of a torch, too.

23:12.680 --> 23:13.670
Huh?

23:14.500 --> 23:16.380
What are you after?

23:16.380 --> 23:17.720
Ah...

23:17.720 --> 23:21.120
Okay, are you willing to listen 
to a long story, then?

23:21.120 --> 23:22.440
A long story?

23:22.440 --> 23:23.180
Yeah.

23:23.900 --> 23:26.000
When a warrior gives someone a magic weapon,

23:26.000 --> 23:29.540
it's customary to explain 
its history, after all.

23:30.690 --> 23:35.150
Are you listening? That dagger was 
forged by dwarfs in ancient times,

23:35.150 --> 23:38.710
and was used to slay a chimera 
and pierce a dragon's scales...
